# LAMMPS reference: GCMC (Grand Canonical Monte Carlo) for adsorption
# Replace __STRUCTURE_FILE__, molecule file if used, T (temperature), mu (chemical potential eV), and pair settings.
# fix gcmc: N = perform GCMC every N steps, X = number of exchange attempts per step, M = MC move steps, type = molecule type, seed = random seed, T = temp, mu = chemical potential (eV), displace = max displacement.
# For molecular GCMC use atom_style full and molecule command; for atomic use atom_style atomic.

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

read_data __STRUCTURE_FILE__

pair_style lj/cut 12.0
pair_coeff 1 1 0.238 3.40
pair_coeff 2 2 0.238 3.40
pair_coeff 1 2 0.238 3.40

# If using molecules (uncomment and set molecule file)
# molecule mol1 __MOLECULE_FILE__
# mass 2 16.0

# GCMC fix: 100 steps between attempts, 100 exchanges per attempt, 0 insert/delete, type 1, seed, T (K), mu (eV), displace 0.1
fix fgcmc all gcmc 100 100 0 1 12345 __T__ __MU__ 0.1

thermo 500
thermo_style custom step temp pe atoms

run 100000

unfix fgcmc
